{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44115738",
      "title": "ViewChild vs ContentChild",
      "lectureOrder": 134,
      "videoOrder": 128,
      "sourceHash": "938fc1682f422b44a998fce05cd53c63d4075fa34b236ec995ddba36891fb8ff",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.72,
          "end": 2.247,
          "en": "So you'll learn about",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.247,
          "end": 4.71,
          "en": "viewChild and viewChildren.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 4.71,
          "end": 8.79,
          "en": "Both the decorator version and this functional version.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.79,
          "end": 13.17,
          "en": "There also are a related decorator and a related function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.17,
          "end": 16.41,
          "en": "that can also sometimes come in handy.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.41,
          "end": 19.56,
          "en": "And for that I'll go to that ControlComponent",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.56,
          "end": 21.363,
          "en": "that we created earlier.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.86,
          "end": 25.32,
          "en": "In there, I'm using ng-content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.32,
          "end": 29.31,
          "en": "to output any input or text area elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.31,
          "end": 32.133,
          "en": "that are wrapped by this ControlComponent.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 33.51,
          "end": 38.51,
          "en": "Now what if you wanted to get hold of those input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 38.61,
          "end": 40.41,
          "en": "or text area elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 40.41,
          "end": 44.64,
          "en": "inside of your ControlComponent class?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 44.64,
          "end": 48.39,
          "en": "Well, you can't use viewChild for that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 48.39,
          "end": 52.68,
          "en": "because if you are using ng-content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 52.68,
          "end": 57.24,
          "en": "for projecting content into this template,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 57.24,
          "end": 62.24,
          "en": "the projected content is not actually part of the template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 62.61,
          "end": 65.25,
          "en": "And the viewChild and the viewChildren",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 65.25,
          "end": 67.71,
          "en": "only allows you to select content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 67.71,
          "end": 70.14,
          "en": "that is part of the template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 70.14,
          "end": 74.22,
          "en": "So put in our words where the code is in that template,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 74.22,
          "end": 77.493,
          "en": "not the placeholder for it as it's the case here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 78.78,
          "end": 82.26,
          "en": "But Angular gives you a way of getting hold",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 82.26,
          "end": 84.423,
          "en": "of that projected content.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 85.32,
          "end": 90.32,
          "en": "With help of the ContentChild or ContentChildren decorators",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 91.71000000000001,
          "end": 96.423,
          "en": "or the ContentChild and ContentChildren functions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 97.44,
          "end": 100.68299999999999,
          "en": "And I'll start with the decorator ContentChild.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 102.21000000000001,
          "end": 105.87,
          "en": "It essentially works like the viewChild decorator.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 105.87,
          "end": 108.09,
          "en": "You put it in front of a property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 108.09,
          "end": 112.47,
          "en": "that can be marked as private, but that's not required.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 112.47,
          "end": 115.65299999999999,
          "en": "And you can give that property any name of your choice.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 116.49000000000001,
          "end": 118.35,
          "en": "And here I'll simply name it control,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 118.35,
          "end": 120.93,
          "en": "but it is up to you as mentioned.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 120.93,
          "end": 125.93,
          "en": "Now, just as viewChild, ContentChild now needs a selector",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 126.33,
          "end": 130.2,
          "en": "to find the content element that should be selected",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 130.2,
          "end": 131.973,
          "en": "and stored in control here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 132.87,
          "end": 137.19,
          "en": "And just as before, you could use a component class name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 137.19,
          "end": 140.01,
          "en": "or a directive class name here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 140.01,
          "end": 143.973,
          "en": "or you could use a template variable, for example, input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 146.28,
          "end": 149.19,
          "en": "Now I'll set the type of control in just a second.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 149.19,
          "end": 150.6,
          "en": "First, I wanna make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 150.6,
          "end": 154.173,
          "en": "that this input variable exists in some template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 155.22,
          "end": 157.44,
          "en": "Now the template we wanna manipulate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 157.44,
          "end": 160.47,
          "en": "and to which we want to add that template variable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 160.47,
          "end": 163.32,
          "en": "is not this ControlComponent template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 163.32,
          "end": 165.99,
          "en": "Because in here we just have the placeholder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 165.99,
          "end": 169.44,
          "en": "for the eventually projected content.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 169.44,
          "end": 171.63,
          "en": "So instead we have to go to the place",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 171.63,
          "end": 175.44,
          "en": "where those elements are indeed set up,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 175.44,
          "end": 178.773,
          "en": "which is the NewTicketComponent HTML file in my case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 179.64,
          "end": 183.87,
          "en": "Here I'm passing input and text area into app-control,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 183.87,
          "end": 185.07,
          "en": "which is that component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 185.07,
          "end": 186.813,
          "en": "where I just added ContentChild.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 188.37,
          "end": 190.29,
          "en": "Well, and it's now here where we can",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 190.29,
          "end": 193.17,
          "en": "add input as a variable name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 193.17,
          "end": 196.68,
          "en": "to the input and the text area elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 196.68,
          "end": 200.16,
          "en": "And you can use the same template variable named twice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 200.16,
          "end": 201.42000000000002,
          "en": "as you see here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 201.42000000000002,
          "end": 204.39,
          "en": "And you can also add multiple template variables",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 204.39,
          "end": 206.913,
          "en": "to those elements as you can see.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 208.2,
          "end": 211.05,
          "en": "But with that, I'm adding this input variable here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 211.05,
          "end": 213.9,
          "en": "and back into ControlComponent TypeScript file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 213.9,
          "end": 216.32999999999998,
          "en": "I'm selecting projected content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 216.32999999999998,
          "end": 220.203,
          "en": "by looking for that template variable named input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 221.25,
          "end": 223.44,
          "en": "And therefore I know that control",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 223.44,
          "end": 228.24,
          "en": "in this app ControlComponent will then be an ElementRef.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 228.24,
          "end": 231.27,
          "en": "So that should be used as a type here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 231.27,
          "end": 234.393,
          "en": "and should be imported from at Angular core.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 235.35,
          "end": 237.81,
          "en": "And eventually in that ElementRef",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 237.81,
          "end": 239.46,
          "en": "I'll get hold of an HTMLInputElement",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 241.89,
          "end": 244.053,
          "en": "or an HTMLTextAreaElement.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 247.26,
          "end": 249.27,
          "en": "Because I know that both kinds of elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 249.27,
          "end": 252.61,
          "en": "can be projected into this ControlComponent.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 253.56,
          "end": 257.67,
          "en": "Now I'm using ContentChild instead of ContentChildren here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 257.67,
          "end": 261.3,
          "en": "even though multiple elements have that input variable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 261.3,
          "end": 265.32,
          "en": "because in each instance of my ControlComponent",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 265.32,
          "end": 269.04,
          "en": "there will only be one input or text area.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 269.04,
          "end": 272.79,
          "en": "I'm only passing one input or text area element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 272.79,
          "end": 275.58299999999997,
          "en": "per app ControlComponent instance.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 277.86,
          "end": 280.26,
          "en": "That's why inside that ControlComponent,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 280.26,
          "end": 282.363,
          "en": "it's ContentChild not ContentChildren.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 284.43,
          "end": 285.57,
          "en": "Now just as before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 285.57,
          "end": 289.2,
          "en": "control could be undefined if nothing's found.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 289.2,
          "end": 292.65,
          "en": "But with that we can then console log this control",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 292.65,
          "end": 295.503,
          "en": "for example, whenever the control is clicked.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 296.67,
          "end": 299.19,
          "en": "Well, and with that you should see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 299.19,
          "end": 301.5,
          "en": "that if I click on that input here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 301.5,
          "end": 303.39,
          "en": "the ElementRef is output.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 303.39,
          "end": 306.813,
          "en": "And you see in the nativeElement I got this input element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 308.4,
          "end": 311.55,
          "en": "If on the other hand I click on that text area,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 311.55,
          "end": 315.69,
          "en": "you see the selected element is that text area element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 315.69,
          "end": 318.003,
          "en": "that's text area dom object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 318.96,
          "end": 322.56,
          "en": "And that's how you could get hold of projected content.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 322.56,
          "end": 324.78,
          "en": "Instead of elements that are defined",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 324.78,
          "end": 326.973,
          "en": "right inside of that template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 328.02,
          "end": 329.94,
          "en": "Now, just as with viewChild,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 329.94,
          "end": 333.21,
          "en": "there also is a function and signal alternative",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 333.21,
          "end": 337.89,
          "en": "if you're using Angular 17.3 or later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 337.89,
          "end": 341.58,
          "en": "Because you can also set up this control property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 341.58,
          "end": 345.84000000000003,
          "en": "by using the ContentChild function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 345.84000000000003,
          "end": 348.93,
          "en": "or ContentChildren if you would try",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 348.93,
          "end": 351.573,
          "en": "to select multiple projected elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 353.34000000000003,
          "end": 356.25,
          "en": "Now again, you must pass your selector,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 356.25,
          "end": 360.543,
          "en": "in this case, the template variable name to ContentChild.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 361.86,
          "end": 364.65,
          "en": "And you should add this extra type annotation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 364.65,
          "end": 366.03,
          "en": "with angle brackets",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 366.03,
          "end": 369.93,
          "en": "and make it clear that in there we'll get an ElementRef",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 369.93,
          "end": 372.27,
          "en": "which then will actually refer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 372.27,
          "end": 376.563,
          "en": "or hold an input element or a text area element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 378.48,
          "end": 380.85,
          "en": "So that's how you can tell TypeScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 380.85,
          "end": 384.06,
          "en": "which kind of value will eventually end up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 384.06,
          "end": 386.79,
          "en": "in this control Signal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 386.79,
          "end": 388.17,
          "en": "And since it is a Signal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 388.17,
          "end": 391.71,
          "en": "you also must execute control as a function down there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 391.71,
          "end": 394.443,
          "en": "to read that Signal value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 395.37,
          "end": 399.24,
          "en": "With that, if you reload, if you click on the title input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 399.24,
          "end": 403.17,
          "en": "you output that ElementRef that refers to that title input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 403.17,
          "end": 406.38,
          "en": "And if you click on the Request text area,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 406.38,
          "end": 410.64,
          "en": "you get that object in your ElementRef.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 410.64,
          "end": 412.40999999999997,
          "en": "So that's working the way it should.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 412.40999999999997,
          "end": 416.373,
          "en": "Now with this alternative ContentChild function.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
